{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T09:36:58-07:00","id":1376818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375760-all-details-about-baali?p=1376793#post1376793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Catch is, ur-Shulgi has a known Banu Haqim childe, al-Ashrad, meaning it can't belong to the main Baali bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I also don't see this as precluding Ur-Shulgi from being the Unnamed. Nergal and Moloch are said to get rather upset when the Unnamed is mentioned to them, and Ur-Shulgi played a big role in ending either the First or Second Baali War. I'm confident Ur-Shulgi was intended to be the Unnamed, but White Wolf provided enough wiggle room for storytellers to make it someone else if they wanted.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12142\" data-vbnamecard=\"12142\">Undead rabbit</a> did a great job of providing a lot of detail regarding the Baali, some of which I'd missed myself when compiling together their various mysteries and trying to suss out their most likely origins truths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","user":"Archasimos","date":". 03-27-2020, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T10:29:41-07:00","id":1376821,"title":"","content":"I do not believe it to be beyond Ur-Shulgi to choose which of his Childer to be of Haquim's House and which to be of the House of Ashur. Haquim embraced what seemed to be a Shepard boy already infested with a demon, a ferectoi in my headcanon, and chucked into the pit. Even if he was only a Banu Haquim he could blend with the Baali because he was already cursed by diabolism which would make perfect camouflage. If his childer were embraced and weren't Baali all he would need to do would be to enact the apostacy ritual in secret, he may have invented it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T11:30:12-07:00","id":1376831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375760-all-details-about-baali?p=1376821#post1376821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not believe it to be beyond Ur-Shulgi to choose which of his Childer to be of Haquim's House and which to be of the House of Ashur. Haquim embraced what seemed to be a Shepard boy already infested with a demon, a ferectoi in my headcanon, and chucked into the pit. Even if he was only a Banu Haquim he could blend with the Baali because he was already cursed by diabolism which would make perfect camouflage. If his childer were embraced and weren't Baali all he would need to do would be to enact the apostacy ritual in secret, he may have invented it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the nature of his embrace, I see no reason why Ur-Shulgi's childer would need to also be Baali. Assuming he's the Unnamed, he has a different sire than Nergal and Moloch. Despite the story about Nergal, Moloch and the Unnamed crawling from the Well of Ashur, it's entirely possible they didn't all receive the embrace or crawl out of the well at the same time.<br /> <br /> While Clanbook Baali mentions a Cainite of great power and majesty found the well of Ashur one night, it could have actually been several antediluvians, an idea I've toyed with. Clanbook Baali describes an array of powers that the Cainite possessed, and while even a relatively young antediluvian might possess them all, I think it lends credence to there being multiple antediluvians present. Saulot, along with Tzimisce, may have both bled into the well. Haqim might have been present (either known or unbeknownst to those who bled into the well), which could explain his knowledge of the well's location and function. Then he later returned, embraced Ur-Shulgi, and tossed him into the well. Ur-Shulgi's mastery of Blood Sorcery in what appears to be a relatively short time could very well be explained by him being a Widderslainte.<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi became the leader of the Baali during that time, and led them in open war against the other clans (which is what Haqim wanted). The Baali were defeated (though obviously not entirely destroyed). Afterwards (or perhaps during/near the end of the battle), Haqim supposedly tore the demon or whatever it was from Ur-Shulgi, but even after doing so, there was an infernal taint left behind. I suspect that even Ur-Shulgi himself was unaware of this for a good while, so it may not have been evident to others until it began to take hold of him/it. Later, Haqim lied about Ur-Shulgi's embrace, and claimed he had found the boy dying on the battlefield and the Embrace was the only way to save that innocent victim.<br /> <br /> What I love about all this and the rest of the Baali lore (much of the World of Darkness lore really) is that it's laced with hints and clues and plot hooks that inspire a variety of ways to use the Baali and their origins in all of our stories (without requiring us to come up with it all ourselves). The same storyteller could run two separate campaigns that involve the Baali, switch up some of their lore, and be able to keep to them mysterious even to players well versed in the Baali's lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","user":"Archasimos","date":". 04-05-2020, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T11:45:09-07:00","id":1376833,"title":"","content":"I got into this in the Refrigerator Thoughts on Saulot thread, but here's what I've been doing in my current Dark Ages game. Obviously none of this is canonical. I also haven't really revealed that much of it to my group, yet.<br /> <br /> In the East Saulot split his Hun and P'o, so his P'o could go about doing good works, preaching Golconda and be a perfect being. His Hun was allowed to exist to do what was necessary, like found the Baali.<br /> <br /> The Baali actually have a purpose and that's to keep performing atrocities to keep the sleeping Children from waking up. It's performing relatively minor evils to prevent cataclysmic levels of destruction from happening. The atrocities keep the ancient demons dreaming. They also serve as a means of unifying the rest of the Kindred and for a time at least turn them away from their petty Jyhads.<br /> <br /> The Watcher caste of the Salubri serves as model to build the third group of Baali descended from the nameless one. This third group is supposed to keep an eye on the other Baali to make sure they play their role and don't go too far. Whenever one of them gets it into their head that it'd be a good idea to wake up one of the sleeping Children, the nameless ones step in. They either influence events so the rest of kindred society becomes aware of the Baali plot or they intervene directly and destroy them. So it was the Baali watcher group that influenced the Assamites and Salubri to attack Chorazin and pushed the Ventrue in Rome to attack Carthage.<br /> <br /> I haven't really fully fleshed out some of the mechanics for the Watcher Baali, but have the one the group encountered using a modified Valeran that has a variation of Ending The Watch that works on unwilling subjects, including kindred. This lends some real gravity to the stories of Salubri being soul stealers and it not being purely Tremere propaganda. For a discipline spread they get the modified Valeran and Damonion. I'm on the fence if they'd have Obfuscate or Auspex for another discipline. I suppose since it's an NPC only group, mainly populated by very old vampires, I could give them both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T12:07:41-07:00","id":1376837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375760-all-details-about-baali?p=1376833#post1376833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got into this in the Refrigerator Thoughts on Saulot thread, but here's what I've been doing in my current Dark Ages game. Obviously none of this is canonical. I also haven't really revealed that much of it to my group, yet.<br /> <br /> In the East Saulot split his Hun and P'o, so his P'o could go about doing good works, preaching Golconda and be a perfect being. His Hun was allowed to exist to do what was necessary, like found the Baali.<br /> <br /> The Baali actually have a purpose and that's to keep performing atrocities to keep the sleeping Children from waking up. It's performing relatively minor evils to prevent cataclysmic levels of destruction from happening. The atrocities keep the ancient demons dreaming. They also serve as a means of unifying the rest of the Kindred and for a time at least turn them away from their petty Jyhads.<br /> <br /> The Watcher caste of the Salubri serves as model to build the third group of Baali descended from the nameless one. This third group is supposed to keep an eye on the other Baali to make sure they play their role and don't go too far. Whenever one of them gets it into their head that it'd be a good idea to wake up one of the sleeping Children, the nameless ones step in. They either influence events so the rest of kindred society becomes aware of the Baali plot or they intervene directly and destroy them. So it was the Baali watcher group that influenced the Assamites and Salubri to attack Chorazin and pushed the Ventrue in Rome to attack Carthage.<br /> <br /> I haven't really fully fleshed out some of the mechanics for the Watcher Baali, but have the one the group encountered using a modified Valeran that has a variation of Ending The Watch that works on unwilling subjects, including kindred. This lends some real gravity to the stories of Salubri being soul stealers and it not being purely Tremere propaganda. For a discipline spread they get the modified Valeran and Damonion. I'm on the fence if they'd have Obfuscate or Auspex for another discipline. I suppose since it's an NPC only group, mainly populated by very old vampires, I could give them both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Auspex would be more appropriate. It sounds like they could exist less from hiding but more from people not knowing what they secretly are. They could still have obfuscate learned out of cost. I mean they are called the Watchers... they need Auspex Man!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T12:21:34-07:00","id":1376838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375760-all-details-about-baali?p=1376837#post1376837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Auspex would be more appropriate. It sounds like they could exist less from hiding but more from people not knowing what they secretly are. They could still have obfuscate learned out of cost. I mean they are called the Watchers... they need Auspex Man!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya, I'm on the fence on that one, especially since watcher Salubri have both. On the one hand they need Auspex to find the hidden, on the other they need Obfuscate to remain undetected. I guess Damonion is the least necessary for them to serve their purpose, but then they don't feel like Baali without it. For my purposes it doesn't really matter since they're NPCs and old enough they could have learned the out of clan discipline anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T13:06:24-07:00","id":1376846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375760-all-details-about-baali?p=1376818#post1376818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also don't see this as precluding Ur-Shulgi from being the Unnamed. Nergal and Moloch are said to get rather upset when the Unnamed is mentioned to them, and Ur-Shulgi played a big role in ending either the First or Second Baali War. I'm confident Ur-Shulgi was intended to be the Unnamed, but White Wolf provided enough wiggle room for storytellers to make it someone else if they wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly dubious of claiming that ur-Shulgi as the Unnamed was the original intent, because at the time it was created, Haqim wasn't in the running as the possible Baali progenitor, nor were the books pushing the idea of multiple Baali progenitors.<br /> <br /> That there's something shady and Baali-connected about ur-Shulgi, yes - that they were the third of the original Baali 4th Gens, no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T13:12:37-07:00","id":1376847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375760-all-details-about-baali?p=1376846#post1376846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm honestly dubious of claiming that ur-Shulgi as the Unnamed was the original intent, because at the time it was created, Haqim wasn't in the running as the possible Baali progenitor, nor were the books pushing the idea of multiple Baali progenitors.<br /> <br /> That there's something shady and Baali-connected about ur-Shulgi, yes - that they were the third of the original Baali 4th Gens, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>The running was just Saulot and Cappadocius though, and that's a lot more boring than the increased ambiguity. It was during the Talmaherah book that realized they should full on commit to the ambiguity, and they tossed in a narrator perspective of Tzimisce embracing the first Baali, which contradicted the other stories and introducing the idea of Ashur being the Location rather then the Sire. And then in the Beckett book introducing the notion Ashur was a state of being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T13:33:30-07:00","id":1376850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375760-all-details-about-baali?p=1376846#post1376846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm honestly dubious of claiming that ur-Shulgi as the Unnamed was the original intent, because at the time it was created, Haqim wasn't in the running as the possible Baali progenitor, nor were the books pushing the idea of multiple Baali progenitors.<br /> <br /> That there's something shady and Baali-connected about ur-Shulgi, yes - that they were the third of the original Baali 4th Gens, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>While there's no explicit evidence they were pushing the idea of multiple progenitors for the Baali at the time, I feel there's enough evidence gathered by reading between the lines to support it in any stories someone wants to run (not that anyone has to adhere to canon in the first place). That being said, the bulk of the Baali seem to descend from Moloch and Nergal, and whichever antediluvians spawned them, while in the scenario I presented, Haqim sired Ur-Shulgi/ The Unnamed but not Moloch and Nergal, and while Ur-Shulgi has sired Banu Haqim childer, it doesn't appear to have contributed childer to the Baali (unless he sired them during the time he led the Baali in the war), or in secret in the years since, but I haven't seen any evidence of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","user":"Archasimos","date":". 03-27-2020, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T14:18:48-07:00","id":1376854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375760-all-details-about-baali?p=1376847#post1376847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The running was just Saulot and Cappadocius though, and that's a lot more boring than the increased ambiguity. It was during the Talmaherah book that realized they should full on commit to the ambiguity, and they tossed in a narrator perspective of Tzimisce embracing the first Baali, which contradicted the other stories and introducing the idea of Ashur being the Location rather then the Sire. And then in the Beckett book introducing the notion Ashur was a state of being.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was content enough up to revised on how they portrayed the Baali. Presenting ur-Shulgi in both Children of the Night, Clanbook Assamite Revised and the novel was a great idea. The horror ur-Shulgi imposed to the Assamites back in the day was an amazing story seed for any game. Having ur-Shulgi being something other than one of the oldest 4th generation Assamite sorcerers, takes what he once was meant to be. Of course, any crafty ST can work around such idea if one wants to have him as the Unnamed, but I feel like it is STs laziness to just use ur-Shulgi and don't create a story around someone else with a unique background and motives.<br /> <br /> V20 started being canon agnostic which was a perfect way of not complicating things more than they already were, the ambiguity between 2nd ed and revised was a good thing. When V20 decided that their canon material was to re-writing everything and any V20 was now the true canon of everything, was where they actually missed the point of having V20 being canon agnostic. By rewriting everything, they not only lost the value of 20 years of historical ambiguity but create even more question I believe that even they weren't aware of (questions and plots they had to justify in the later books of V20 (Black Hand, Lore of Clans, Lore of Bloodlines, Beckett Jyhad Diary). For new people, it is easier to start up from there. To us old ones, it just tip over our setting to hell (to those who are OCD on the setting and MUST have everything as perfect as possible). Understandable, we are few.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 03-27-2020, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T14:34:18-07:00","id":1376857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375760-all-details-about-baali?p=1376854#post1376854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was content enough up to revised on how they portrayed the Baali. Presenting ur-Shulgi in both Children of the Night, Clanbook Assamite Revised and the novel was a great idea. The horror ur-Shulgi imposed to the Assamites back in the day was an amazing story seed for any game. Having ur-Shulgi being something other than one of the oldest 4th generation Assamite sorcerers, takes what he once was meant to be. Of course, any crafty ST can work around such idea if one wants to have him as the Unnamed, but I feel like it is STs laziness to just use ur-Shulgi and don't create a story around someone else with a unique background and motives.<br /> <br /> V20 started being canon agnostic which was a perfect way of not complicating things more than they already were, the ambiguity between 2nd ed and revised was a good thing. When V20 decided that their canon material was to re-writing everything and any V20 was now the true canon of everything, was where they actually missed the point of having V20 being canon agnostic. By rewriting everything, they not only lost the value of 20 years of historical ambiguity but create even more question I believe that even they weren't aware of (questions and plots they had to justify in the later books of V20 (Black Hand, Lore of Clans, Lore of Bloodlines, Beckett Jyhad Diary). For new people, it is easier to start up from there. To us old ones, it just tip over our setting to hell (to those who are OCD on the setting and MUST have everything as perfect as possible). Understandable, we are few.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>I really wouldn't call using Ur-Shulgi as the Unnamed lazy. Unless they're winging everything, storytellers often already have enough work on their hands. While it's out of the ordinary for me, I've written 120 pages of preludes for the players of the V5 Dark Ages game I'm running for them to play through. While I'd likely still write a fair bit of my own material for it, I'll happy use existing material to lessen the load of the games I run. The first story I'm running them through is Fountains of Bright Crimson, though I'm modifying it to suit my Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T14:57:57-07:00","id":1376861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375760-all-details-about-baali?p=1376857#post1376857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really wouldn't call using Ur-Shulgi as the Unnamed lazy. Unless they're winging everything, storytellers often already have enough work on their hands. While it's out of the ordinary for me, I've written 120 pages of preludes for the players of the V5 Dark Ages game I'm running for them to play through. While I'd likely still write a fair bit of my own material for it, I'll happy use existing material to lessen the load of the games I run. The first story I'm running them through is Fountains of Bright Crimson, though I'm modifying it to suit my Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you on the expanded preludes and settings of what already exists. Such thing has been a hobby of mine for 20 years at least. I too suit modules to my chronicles, even have the PCs live the event through different POV than protagonists or antagonists. Sometimes I set them work an event around what happened (like the Great Leap Outward from Kindred of the East, I used the prelude from Night of Prophecy, the one that turned out as failure due to the Sixth Maelstrom).<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T18:25:31-07:00","id":1378895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375760-all-details-about-baali?p=1376447#post1376447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Flood&quot;:<br /> Historical accuracy: The disappearance of the Clovis culture is being recently tied to the Younger Dryas extinction event, which apparently was caused by a meteor impact in Greenland (Hiawatha crater), assumingly causing a massive worldwide rise of the ocean level. This happened in 9500 BC.<br /> <br /> Second City (after the war with the 2nd generation):<br /> Demon-venerating vampire War. Haqim leaves the Second City and returns with the sorcerer caste. For a century, Assamites and Salubri purges every single devil-worshipper in the Second City.<br /> [Cb-AR, pg. 10]<br /> <br /> &quot;Second City&quot; (half a millennium later):<br /> The first tribe establishes the Well of Sacrifices in Assur. Saulot destroys it and embraces the Three Baali progenitors.<br /> [Cb-Ba, pg. 15-16]<br /> A surrounding city dies. The new adversary are called the Baali. Mancheaka leads the attack but she and her brood perishes. Survivors retreat to a cave and there they meet ur-Shulgi for the first time.<br /> [Cb-AR, pg. 12-13]<br /> <br /> 4000 BC:<br /> Historical accuracy: Nergal is the patron god of Mashkan-shapir and Kutha. Ereshkigal also is the patron goddess of Kutha.<br /> <br /> 3100 BC:<br /> 1st attempt to awaken Namtaru. Nergal was the God of Mashkan-shapir. He believed that a Child slept beneath the city and sacrificed the entire city mortals to rise him. Only the betrayal of his D'habi ghoul family and the powers of the Lasombra priests of Ereshkigal that flooded the city with abyssal darkness, prevented Nergal from arising Namtaru.<br /> Historical accuracy: There is no known previous record of Mashkan-shapir during the Uruk period (4000 BC to 3100 BC) other than it was known that the city was occupied. Historical records begin during the Akkad period (2334 BC - 2154 BC).<br /> [Cb-Ba, pg. 18-19]<br /> <br /> 2050 BC:<br /> Historical accuracy: Ashur becomes the god of the city Assur (Qal'at Sherqat). The Assyrian Empire begin to expand to the west into the lands of Anatolia.<br /> [Cb-C, pg. 12] [Cb-Ba, pg. 17]<br /> <br /> 2000 BC (aprox):<br /> Nergal appears in the city of Assur using the name &quot;Shaitan&quot;. Learns that the Namtaru resting place is beneath Chorazim. Shaitan builds a temple in the city, finds Namtaru's body and takes it to Crete.<br /> [Cb-Ba, pg. 21]<br /> Mi-ka-il is taken away from Ebla during the day and is taken to Kish, leaving Ma-ri behind.<br /> Historical accuracy: The city of Ebla is destroyed between 2050 BC and 1950 BC, though reasons remain unknown.<br /> [CtbN, pg. 103]<br /> <br /> 1590 BC (aprox):<br /> Shaitan embraces Cybele.<br /> [Cb-Ba, pg. 66]<br /> Shaitan demands of tribute awakens Set. Menele, still a mortal hero in Athens went, Balthazar from India, Gangrel from the steppes, the Dionysian and his bacchante followers, the Lasombra and Toreador from Africa, all came to face the Baali. He is betrayed by his childe Hay-Tau.<br /> Shaitan's last attempt to &quot;Open the Way&quot; in the Knossos labyrinth. For nine nights and days the Clans unite to stop Shaitan. Set's childer creates a cataclysm to sink the entire island.<br /> Historical accuracy: The Minoan eruption of Thera, one of the largest volcanic eruptions in history. Dated between 1642 BC and 1540 BC.<br /> [DAC, pg. 170-171] [Cb-Ba, pg. 24]<br /> <br /> 1100 BC (aprox):<br /> Moloch embraces Annazir.<br /> [VoN, pg. 205]<br /> <br /> 850 BC (aprox):<br /> Tanith embraces Sahar in Tyre.<br /> [DA: RoS, pg. 91]<br /> <br /> 218 BC-202 BC<br /> Cybele aids the Roman Ventrue to defeat Hannibal.<br /> Historical accuracy: Hannibal campaign during the Second Punic War took place from May/June 218 BC until the Battle of Zama in 202 BC.<br /> [Cb-Ba, pg. 66]<br /> <br /> 200 BC (aprox):<br /> Cybele suffers from a blood lust decimating the temples of her followers.<br /> [Cb-Ba, pg. 66]<br /> <br /> 195 BC:<br /> Tanitbaal-Sahar embraces Sahar-Hannibal in Tyre.<br /> [V20TBH, pg. 225]<br /> <br /> 147 BC:<br /> Tanitbaal-Sahar receives summons from his sire in Tyre. He departs from Ostia but never arrived. He disappears from the pages of history.<br /> [DA: RoS, pg. 92]<br /> <br /> 146 BC:<br /> Troile and Moloch melt into the ground, Carthage. Cybele seals them in the earth.<br /> [Cb-Ba, pg. 23, pg. 67]<br /> <br /> 541:<br /> Hay-Tau worship of Namtaru unleashes a plague in Egypt.<br /> Historical accuracy: Bubonic plague appears in the port of Pelusium, Egypt and spreads to Alexandria and Constantinople.<br /> [Cb-Ba, pg. 24]<br /> <br /> 636: (for some unknown reason, the date is changed to 646 in V20DA)<br /> Samiel makes a stop in a village en route to Chorazim. There he embraces Qawiyya el-Ghaduba and leaves her a first-hand copy of the Code of Samiel.<br /> [DA: RoH, pg. 92]<br /> Assamite warriors war on the Baali. As the Baali retreated to Chorazim, they capture Izhim abd'Azrael. Enraged, the warrior caste assault Chorazim. They find Izhim being focus of a ritual that cursed them as follows: &quot;As you thirst for our blood, so you shall hunger for all blood for all time&quot;.<br /> [LS3-WatD, pg. 53] [Cb-AR, pg. 23] [TCCA, pg. 111-119]<br /> <br /> 681:<br /> Sugareg embraces Maureen in Barqa.<br /> [AT, pg. 78]<br /> <br /> 1193:<br /> Mannal, childe of Sultan Darshuf, plots with the Bashirite and to bring the Banu Haqim and destroy the Baali of Damascus.<br /> [VoN, pg. 196]<br /> <br /> 1242:<br /> Izhim ur-Baal sacrifices his childe, Enkara to Namtaru in Chorazim.<br /> [TCCA, pg. 111-119]<br /> <br /> 1260:<br /> Muhandis betrays his sire, Sultan Darshuf and his vizier Annazir, and joins the mongol Gangrel to destroy the Baali in Damascus.<br /> Historical accuracy: Kitbuqa takes Damascus on March 1, 1260.<br /> [CabN, pg. 132]<br /> <br /> These are some of the dates relevant to the Baali I compiled.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I rather like this particular timeline you posted, especially the suggested date of the Second City being around the time of the Clovis Culter, and that the Flood could have been caused by a meteor or comet. The date of 9500 B.C.E. or thereabouts for the Second City lines up much better with the ages and implied embrace dates of characters like Ur-Shulgi, Nergal, Moloch, as well as the dates of certain events like the First Baali War, which is most often said to have taken place during the time of the Second City, rather than the time of the First City. I've always felt that the First City existed somewhere in the neighborhood of 11,000 B.C.E., give or take a millennium, and that the Second City existed around 9500 B.C.E., especially with the antediluvians being said in a few places to be AT LEAST 10,000 years old, if not older.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T16:46:18-07:00","id":1379353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375760-all-details-about-baali?p=1378895#post1378895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I rather like this particular timeline you posted, especially the suggested date of the Second City being around the time of the Clovis Culter, and that the Flood could have been caused by a meteor or comet. The date of 9500 B.C.E. or thereabouts for the Second City lines up much better with the ages and implied embrace dates of characters like Ur-Shulgi, Nergal, Moloch, as well as the dates of certain events like the First Baali War, which is most often said to have taken place during the time of the Second City, rather than the time of the First City. I've always felt that the First City existed somewhere in the neighborhood of 11,000 B.C.E., give or take a millennium, and that the Second City existed around 9500 B.C.E., especially with the antediluvians being said in a few places to be AT LEAST 10,000 years old, if not older.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes I too consider First City to be at least from 10000 BC which probably prospered for millennia before the flood. I tried not to specify dates on this particular subject (though I do have them in my headcanon) to not confuse the OP who asked for this.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T11:02:05-07:00","id":1380420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375760-all-details-about-baali?p=1376831#post1376831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I love about all this and the rest of the Baali lore (much of the World of Darkness lore really) is that it's laced with hints and clues and plot hooks that inspire a variety of ways to use the Baali and their origins in all of our stories (without requiring us to come up with it all ourselves). The same storyteller could run two separate campaigns that involve the Baali, switch up some of their lore, and be able to keep to them mysterious even to players well versed in the Baali's lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a point that can't be emphasized enough. Making use of the gaps in Baali lore to wedge your own ideas in there can be a lovely way to keep the bloodline surprising and scary, or even just put your own stamp of ownership on the world of your games.<br /> <br /> Here's an example: take Ereshkigal. In White Wolf canon, there's a 4th generation Gangrel by this name. She's known for two things. She pursued the Toreador Antedeluvian through ancient Sumeria on Ennoia's behalf in one Toreador oral tradition, and the Lasombra priestesses who fought Nergal at Chorazin worshipped her. And that's all we have on her. She disappears into legend.<br /> <br /> Real world archaeological research tells us that Ereshkigal was the wife of Nergal, that she had a maternal relationship with an entity called Namtar, and that she first came to Nergal's attention when she unleashed Namtar against the other gods. Here, Namtar is a plague spreader, and is clearly the inspiration for the Namtaru entity who is so closely associated with Nergal in World of Darkness lore.<br /> <br /> Did Ereshkigal have a relationship with Nergal long before Moloch would have a similar affair with Troile? Was Namtaru a demon summoned via the darkest of blood sorcery, or a humble earth monster summoned with Song in the Dark (an Animalism power from the Nosferatu clanbooks)?<br /> <br /> And about those Lasombra priestess of Ereshkigal. Did the relationship between the two methusalehs end badly? Did one diablerize the other? Or was Ereshkigal covering her lover's escape? Which vampire was the real mastermind of the pair?<br /> <br /> How much does this matter now? Do you use this as trivia, a passage in an obscure journal that the players find so that they can feel like they've discovered a Deep Dark Secret of the Jyhad (tm)? <br /> <br /> Or is Ereshkigal waking up soon to drench the world in blood and darkness?<br /> <br /> The answers to any and all of these can be your decision. You're left that much room to connect dots in your own way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 04-12-2020, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}